NEWSWORTHY NUMBER

Proportion of pickup truck owners who=E2=80=99ve started using their trucks=
 for side hustles or gig work in the past year, according to a recent surve=
y by parts company American Trucks via (https://www.inc.com/bruce-crumley/7=
-in-10-pickup-owners-are-using-their-trucks-for-side-hustles/91272250?_hsen=
c=3Dp2ANqtz-_eXDFGXEaC49mrHzQ_-910xvG6w8SoZrsHhvIcT5dFC0zrgBZ_FoE0uSBLprcRB=
d8gzgN3VTjwGkEoW_h-uNls15gteA&_hsmi=3D394117559 ) Inc. The flatbed vehicles=
 have apparently aided such lucrative ventures =E2=80=94 e.g., transporting=
 supplies for contractors, hauling trash, and helping farmers =E2=80=94 tha=
t 35% of surveyed truckers say they plan to take the work full-time in the =
next year. The additional cashflow increased respondents=E2=80=99 total ann=
ual incomes by ~20% on average.

Maybe reconsider buying that sedan?

